# ─── apps/web environment ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in any required secrets.
# Most values are intentionally NOT set — the dev server runs entirely against
# the Vite proxy without external config.
#
# Dev URLs use `avantej.localhost` (not plain `localhost`) so cookies don't
# collide with other local projects on different ports. Browsers auto-route
# *.localhost to 127.0.0.1; no /etc/hosts edit required.
#
# Required reading: CONTRIBUTING.md → "Dev setup"

# ─── VITE_SERVER_URL — DO NOT SET LOCALLY ──────────────────────────────────
# Auth client (Better-Auth) and the oRPC client read VITE_SERVER_URL to
# decide where to send /api and /rpc calls. We leave it UNSET in local dev
# so both fall back to window.location.origin (i.e. avantej.localhost:3021),
# which keeps cookies same-site and flows requests through the Vite proxy
# to avantej.localhost:3020.
#
# Setting this to http://localhost:3020 or any cross-origin URL will break
# session cookies on first login (SameSite=Lax cross-site → cookie blocked).
#
# Set this ONLY for staging/prod or a deliberate non-proxy setup:
# VITE_SERVER_URL=https://api.your-staging.example.com

# ─── Stripe.js publishable key ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Per ADR-0012, all dev environments share one Stripe test account ("dev-shared").
# Replace with your own test pk if you need an isolated sandbox.
VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_replace_me

# ─── Optional: override the server URL the Vite proxy targets ──────────────
# Defaults to http://localhost:3020 in vite.config.ts. Only set if your
# wrangler dev server is on a different host/port.
# VITE_LOCAL_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:3020
